    <p>The workflow is drastically simplified: you copy the entire text block from your Amadeus terminal (or any GDS following the <a href="https://amadeus.com" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">standard documentation</a>) and paste it into the platform. The system takes care of reading the classes, schedules, airports, and dates, automatically generating a visual PDF, complete with your logo, ready to be sent. This guarantees that the proposal is understandable, your commissions remain hidden, and every quote is registered in the CRM for proper follow-up.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions about Reading PNRs</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>What data is included in the itinerary line of an Amadeus PNR? <span class="text-magenta">▼</span></summary>
      <p>The itinerary line includes the airline code, flight number, booking class, date, origin and destination airports, booking status (e.g., HK), number of seats, and departure and arrival times.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What does HK mean in an Amadeus booking code? <span class="text-magenta">▼</span></summary>
      <p>HK is the status code that means 'Holds Confirmed'. It indicates that the airline has confirmed the reservation for that specific flight segment.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do I identify the ticketing time limit in a PNR? <span class="text-magenta">▼</span></summary>
      <p>The time limit is found in the 'T' (Ticketing) field. It usually appears with the format TK TL followed by a date, indicating the maximum time to issue the ticket before the airline cancels the seats.</p>
    </details>
